# The web client is served byte-for-byte and several contracts measure it in bytes or read it with
# "\n    " patterns, so the working tree must keep LF even on a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true.
# Without this, a local checkout is ~9 KB larger than the index and multi-line assertions fail for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the product.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
